cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Analysis code for: Retrieval performance over clinical free text is
  heterogeneous with respect to acute physiological derangement
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software and the
  manuscript it accompanies.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Mikkelsen
    given-names: Yngve
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1543-3805
repository-code: https://github.com/REPLACE-ME/REPLACE-ME
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-08-21"
keywords:
  - clinical natural language processing
  - information retrieval
  - text embeddings
  - subgroup performance
  - MIMIC-IV
abstract: >-
  Code to reproduce an evaluation of whether known-item retrieval performance
  over ICU discharge summaries varies with the acute physiological derangement
  of the patient whose record is being retrieved. Thirteen transformer encoders
  and a BM25 baseline are evaluated against a single pooled index, with
  candidate explanations assessed across six groups. Contains no patient data;
  MIMIC-IV and MIMIC-IV-Note must be obtained from PhysioNet under their own
  data use agreements.
